From 74396289de8f5c806737377af80259a7381641ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0176: the evolution chart shows each evolution's
 requirements. With the cursor on a "to" box of the detail view a card takes
 the "from" column's place: care mistakes, weight, the stats (a Rookie's: the
 highest stat) and the bonus (one is enough), "Automatic" for a Fresh's Baby
 II, "?????" for a species not yet raised. In the partner's own tree it adds
 the partner's values, a tick or cross per requirement and N of 4, and the
 lines to the evolutions it meets turn green, the rest dim. The marks are
 evoRequirementsMet's, the function calculateRequirementScore now adds up
 (evolution.c), so the card and the game agree. The card's text borrows the
 overview's rows of the text area and gives them back on close
 (chartCardRelease). The Makefile's default PARTNER_MMD_MAX is 0x18800: the
 card's 4.9 KB left 0x20000 under MIN_HEAP

---
 Makefile             |   8 +-
 include/dw/level.h   |   8 +
 src/main/evolution.c | 119 ++++++-----
 src/main/game_menu.c | 457 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 532 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)

